From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:23:55 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 30/43] Plutonium: agent tool fixes: popups in window
 snapshots, results that say what happened, private tabs marked

- snapshot_window passes on the window's open popups; click_window,
  press_window and act_window say they reach menus and name new windows.
- preview_press and preview_drag say what they did.
- A snapshot's [active] (keyboard focus) reads [focused].
- preview_navigate's status doesn't list itself as busy.
- preview_evaluate is in the action timeline.
- Recordings get their length in their header (WebM Duration, MP4 mvhd/
  tkhd/mdhd/mehd), so players can show and seek them.
- The idle sweep and the tab the user is looking at count a Plutonium
  shell showing the tab.
- The floating preview follows the tab whose cursor the agent moves.
- A private tab shows a mask in its panel tab and a Private badge in the
  floating preview.
- find_apps names the launcher's install when there are several.
